{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nLittle Petya loves training spiders. Petya has a board n\u2009\u00d7\u2009m in size. Each cell of the board initially has a spider sitting on it. After one second Petya chooses a certain action for each spider, and all of them humbly perform its commands. There are 5 possible commands: to stay idle or to move from current cell to some of the four side-neighboring cells (that is, one command for each of the four possible directions). Petya gives the commands so that no spider leaves the field. It is allowed for spiders to pass through each other when they crawl towards each other in opposite directions. All spiders crawl simultaneously and several spiders may end up in one cell. Petya wants to know the maximum possible number of spider-free cells after one second.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final boolean _DEBUG = false;\n\n    private static class Scanner {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public Scanner(BufferedReader _br) {\n            br = _br;\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (Exception e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                    return \"\";\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Scanner scan;\n    static PrintWriter out;\n    static int debugCount = 0;\n\n    static void debug(String msg) {\n        if (_DEBUG && debugCount < 200) {\n            out.println(msg);\n            out.flush();\n            debugCount++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        scan = new Scanner(new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in)));\n        out = new PrintWriter(new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out)));\n        new Main().run();\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    int N, M, pow;\n    int[] counts;\n    int[][][] dp;\n\n    void run() {\n        N = scan.nextInt();\n        M = scan.nextInt();\n        if (N < M) {\n            int t = N;\n            N = M;\n            M = t;\n        }\n        pow = 1 << M;\n        counts = new int[pow];\n        dp = new int[N][pow][pow];\n        for (int[][] layer : dp) {\n            for (int[] row : layer) {\n                Arrays.fill(row, -1);\n            }\n        }\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < pow; mask++) {\n            counts[mask] = Integer.bitCount(mask);\n            if (((mask | (mask << 1) | (mask >> 1)) & (pow - 1)) == (pow - 1)) {\n                dp[0][mask][0] = counts[mask];\n            }\n        }\n        int minSpiders = Integer.MAX_VALUE;\n        for (int row = 0; row < N - 1; row++) {\n            for (int prevMask = 0; prevMask < pow; prevMask++) {\n                for (int prevPrevMask = 0; prevPrevMask < pow; prevPrevMask++) {\n                    if (dp[row][prevMask][prevPrevMask] == -1) continue;\n                    for (int currMask = 0; currMask < pow; currMask++) {\n                        if (((prevMask | (prevMask << 1) | (prevMask >> 1) | prevPrevMask | currMask) & (pow - 1)) == (pow - 1)) {\n                            int newVal = dp[row][prevMask][prevPrevMask] + counts[currMask];\n                            if (dp[row + 1][currMask][prevMask] == -1 || dp[row + 1][currMask][prevMask] > newVal) {\n                                dp[row + 1][currMask][prevMask] = newVal;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        for (int lastMask = 0; lastMask < pow; lastMask++) {\n            for (int secondLastMask = 0; secondLastMask < pow; secondLastMask++) {\n                if (dp[N - 1][lastMask][secondLastMask] != -1 &&\n                    ((lastMask | (lastMask << 1) | (lastMask >> 1) | secondLastMask) & (pow - 1)) == (pow - 1)) {\n                    minSpiders = Math.min(minSpiders, dp[N - 1][lastMask][secondLastMask]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        out.println((N * M) - minSpiders);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final boolean _DEBUG = false;\n\n    private static class Scanner {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public Scanner(BufferedReader _br) {\n            br = _br;\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (Exception e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                    return \"\";\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Scanner scan;\n    static PrintWriter out;\n    static int debugCount = 0;\n\n    static void debug(String msg) {\n        if (_DEBUG && debugCount < 200) {\n            out.println(msg);\n            out.flush();\n            debugCount++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        scan = new Scanner(new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in)));\n        out = new PrintWriter(new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out)));\n        new Main().run();\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    int N, M;\n    int pow;\n    int[][][] dp;\n\n    void run() {\n        N = scan.nextInt();\n        M = scan.nextInt();\n        \n        // Ensure M is the smaller dimension for efficiency\n        if (N < M) {\n            int t = N;\n            N = M;\n            M = t;\n        }\n        \n        pow = 1 << M;\n        // dp[row][currMask][prevMask] = minimum spiders needed to cover up to row with given masks\n        dp = new int[N][pow][pow];\n        for (int[][] layer : dp) {\n            for (int[] row : layer) {\n                Arrays.fill(row, -1);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Initialize first row\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < pow; mask++) {\n            int spiderCount = Integer.bitCount(mask);\n            // Check if mask covers all columns in row 0 (considering row -1 as empty)\n            // A column j is covered if mask has bit j set, or bit j-1 set, or bit j+1 set\n            int covered = mask | (mask << 1) | (mask >> 1);\n            covered &= (pow - 1); // mask to M bits\n            \n            if (covered == (pow - 1)) {\n                dp[0][mask][0] = spiderCount;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Fill DP for subsequent rows\n        for (int row = 0; row < N - 1; row++) {\n            for (int prevMask = 0; prevMask < pow; prevMask++) {\n                for (int prevPrevMask = 0; prevPrevMask < pow; prevPrevMask++) {\n                    if (dp[row][prevMask][prevPrevMask] == -1) continue;\n                    \n                    for (int currMask = 0; currMask < pow; currMask++) {\n                        int spiderCount = Integer.bitCount(currMask);\n                        \n                        // Check if columns are covered considering previous two rows\n                        // For row+1, we need to check coverage for row (current row)\n                        // Coverage for column j in current row depends on:\n                        // - currMask (spiders in current row)\n                        // - prevMask (spiders in previous row)\n                        // - prevPrevMask (spiders in row before previous)\n                        int covered = currMask | (currMask << 1) | (currMask >> 1) |\n                                      prevMask | (prevMask << 1) | (prevMask >> 1) |\n                                      prevPrevMask;\n                        covered &= (pow - 1);\n                        \n                        if (covered == (pow - 1)) {\n                            int newVal = dp[row][prevMask][prevPrevMask] + spiderCount;\n                            if (dp[row + 1][currMask][prevMask] == -1 || \n                                dp[row + 1][currMask][prevMask] > newVal) {\n                                dp[row + 1][currMask][prevMask] = newVal;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Find minimum spiders for last row\n        int minSpiders = Integer.MAX_VALUE;\n        for (int lastMask = 0; lastMask < pow; lastMask++) {\n            for (int secondLastMask = 0; secondLastMask < pow; secondLastMask++) {\n                if (dp[N - 1][lastMask][secondLastMask] != -1) {\n                    // Check if last row is fully covered\n                    int covered = lastMask | (lastMask << 1) | (lastMask >> 1) | secondLastMask;\n                    covered &= (pow - 1);\n                    if (covered == (pow - 1)) {\n                        minSpiders = Math.min(minSpiders, dp[N - 1][lastMask][secondLastMask]);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        out.println((N * M) - minSpiders);\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.9\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.7431014789035544e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.002696055569686e-05, -5.495397272170521e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.125986263010418e-06, -1.3470558769768104e-05, -6.437280717364047e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.935142715112306e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.529942543740617e-06, -4.029192859889008e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.0012454380048438907, -2.50339189733495e-06, -4.6132929128361866e-05, -7.271740287251305e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -3.099436753473128e-06, -7.15255509931